		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4796&amp;p=35330#p35330"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>Has anyone run into a situation where audio is really choppy (picket fencing) on any DMR TG via the hotspot, but perfectly fine when RX/TX on a local DMR repeater? Using the same MMDVM hotspot I have no choppy audio with an Anytone 878 or Alinco MD5 DMR radio. <br><br>Feedback welcome!<br><br>-Paul</div></blockquote><br>This question has been asked many times before on this forum. <br><br>Neither TYT or Baofeng seems to bother to calibrate these radios very accurately.<br><br>Try to calibrate your Hotspot to work with your OpenGD77 radio.<br><br>Alternatively calibrate your OpenGD77 radio to your other 2 radios.<br><br>Calibration functionality is documented in the User Guide<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Jan 24, 2025 1:17 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
